// Real scroll-fade hint for .dr-filter-row -- .dr-filter-row itself (not its
// .dr-filter-buttons child) is the actual horizontally-scrolling element
// (overflow-x:auto lives on the row; .dr-filter-buttons just has
// min-width:max-content so it never wraps, forcing the row to overflow and
// scroll) -- confirmed by walking the real computed styles/clientWidth vs
// scrollWidth at each level rather than assuming from the row's own name.
// Driven by the row's actual scrollWidth/scrollLeft, not a fixed breakpoint,
// so the fade only ever shows when there's real content left to scroll to
// (e.g. the Sort dropdown sitting off the edge of the screen on a phone) and
// disappears once scrolled to the end or once the row is wide enough to show
// everything at once. Idempotent and safe to call after every board render --
// attaches its scroll/resize listeners once per row (__drScrollHintInit
